## Clinical content attribution

The clinical rules encoded in `data/sats_tews.yaml` and
`data/sats_discriminators.yaml` are derived from the **South African Triage
Scale (SATS)**, published by the **Emergency Medicine Society of South Africa
(EMSSA)** — *SATS Training Manual* (2012), <https://emssa.org.za>.

SATS clinical content is **cited, not redistributed wholesale**: only the
machine-necessary thresholds, colour bands and discriminator labels are encoded
as data, and each is attributed through the citation helper (`core/citations.py`,
D-15). The transcription provenance and its residual uncertainty are recorded in
`evidence/sats-verification.md` and `docs/SATS.md`.

## MCP protocol

The owned MCP server is authored with the MCP Python SDK and speaks the current
MCP protocol revision **2026-07-28**, negotiating down to legacy 2025-era
clients automatically (see `STACK.md`).

